The Iterative Model in the Software Engineering develops software through repeated cycles (iterations). Each iteration improves the system by adding or refining features until the final product is complete.
Phases in the Iterative Model
Planning Phase 📋
Identify requirements for the current iteration.
Define goals, scope, and resources for that cycle.
Analysis Phase 🔍
Study and refine the requirements.
Understand system needs and feasibility.
Design Phase 🧩
Create system architecture and component designs.
Plan how features will be implemented in this iteration.
Implementation (Coding) Phase 💻
Developers write code according to the design.
A working part of the system is built.
Testing Phase 🧪
The developed part is tested for bugs and functionality.
Ensures the iteration meets requirements.
Evaluation / Review Phase 🔄
Users and developers review the working product.
Feedback is collected and used to plan the next iteration.
Simple Flow
Planning → Analysis → Design → Implementation → Testing → Evaluation → Next Iteration
🔁 This cycle repeats until the entire system is fully developed.
✅ Key Idea: Each iteration produces a working version of the software, gradually improving the product.

