These are common terms used in Agile / Scrum development.
1. User Story 👤
A user story is a short description of a feature from the user’s perspective.
Format:
As a [user], I want [feature], so that [benefit].
Example:
As a customer, I want to log in to the website so that I can access my account.
Purpose:
Describes what the user needs
Helps developers understand user requirements
2. Epic 📚
An epic is a large user story that cannot be completed in one sprint.
It is usually broken down into multiple smaller user stories.
Example:
Epic: Online Shopping System
User stories under it:
Add items to cart
Make payment
Track order
3. Product Backlog 📋
The product backlog is a complete list of all features, requirements, bug fixes, and improvements needed in the product.
Characteristics:
Managed by the Product Owner
Items are prioritized based on importance
Contains epics, user stories, tasks, bugs
Example items:
User login
Payment integration
Profile update feature
4. Sprint Backlog 🗂️
The sprint backlog is a subset of the product backlog selected for a specific sprint (iteration).
Characteristics:
Contains tasks the team will complete during the sprint
Managed by the development team
Updated daily during the sprint
Example:
If the sprint is 2 weeks, the sprint backlog may include:
Create login page
Implement authentication
Test login functionality

Case: Building an Online Bookstore Website
Step 1: Epic
An epic is a large feature that can be broken down.
Example Epic:
“User Account Management”
Step 2: User Stories
Break the epic into smaller user stories:
As a user, I want to register an account so that I can buy books.
As a user, I want to log in so that I can view my account.
As a user, I want to reset my password so that I can recover my account.
Step 3: Product Backlog
The product backlog is the full list of all features for the bookstore:
Epic: User Account Management
Register account
Login
Password recovery
Epic: Shopping Cart
Add books to cart
Remove books from cart
View total price
Epic: Payment System
Pay with credit card
Pay with PayPal
The product backlog contains everything the product should have, prioritized by importance.
